 {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["code-owner"]}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01QTnVR7AtjXnR9o8xj4PJso", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101}, "name": "merge_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and the fix is merged into main, so it's in for today's release.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` said it used banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. That's why `test_half_even` failed: it expects `2.665` to round to `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit (`08d3cd5986`).\n- **PR:** I opened PR #101 against main. When I opened it, the code-owner review request didn't get added, so I requested it separately.\n- **Merge:** When I merged, the request went to the code owner for approval as policy requires. They approved it (\"Approved. Looks right.\"), and PR #101 is now merged into main.", "type": "text"}]}]}